within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.B_BloodAndBloodFormingOrgans.B02A_Antifibrinolytics.B02AA02_TranexamicAcid;
model TranexamicAcid_Li2021_PD_maximum_lysis
  "sigmoid_emax exposure-response sweep — Li_2021 :: maximum lysis (maximum lysis)"
  extends Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep(
    E0 = 0.97,      // [1; % × 0.01]
    Emax = -0.89,  // [1; % × 0.01]
    EC50 = 0.006,  // [kg/m3; mg/L × 0.001]
    gamma = 8.5,
    exposure_per_s = 0.001);   // 1 mg/L per second
  // imax_as_negative_emax: Imax (Q323) enters SigmoidEmaxSweep as −Emax
  annotation(experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 60, Interval = 0.12),
    Documentation(info = "<html><body><h4>TranexamicAcid_Li2021_PD_maximum_lysis</h4><p>The steady-state exposure-response curve of Li S et al., <i>British journal of clinical pharmacology 87(9):3531–3541</i> 2021 (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1111/bcp.14767\">doi:10.1111/bcp.14767</a>) — maximum lysis [%] against tranexamic acid mg/L — obtained by sweeping the driver instead of simulating a dose. Model family: sigmoid_emax.</p><h4>The parameters, in the paper's terms</h4><pre>  E0    =         97 %        drug-free response (baseline) (baseline lysis, Q324)
  Emax  =         89 %        maximal effect term (maximum inhibition, Q323)
  EC50  =          6 mg/L     exposure at half of the maximal effect term (IC50, Q322)
  gamma =        8.5          Hill coefficient (hill factor, Q325)</pre><p>The algebra is <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep\">SigmoidEmaxSweep</a>; this model only supplies the numbers. The x axis is one mg/L of tranexamic acid per second of simulated time (exposure is in kg/m3): there is no state, no dose and no kinetics — plot <code>response</code> against <code>exposure</code> (or <code>time</code>).</p><h4>What it reproduces</h4><pre>  exposure = 0         response 0.97   (drug-free)
  exposure = EC50 (6 mg/L)  response 0.525
  exposure -> infinity  response 0.08</pre></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Li_2021: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: curated candidate</li></ul></body></html>"));
end TranexamicAcid_Li2021_PD_maximum_lysis;
